  "content": {
    "title": "VCU men’s basketball falls to Illinois in Round of 32 of March Madness tournament",
    "text": "VCU guard Brandon Jennings vies for the ball with Illinois guard Keaton Wagler during the first half in the second round of the NCAA college basketball tournament, Saturday, March 21, 2026, in Greenville, S.C. (AP Photo/Chris Carlson) by: Madelyn Frentress Posted: Mar 22, 2026 / 12:15 AM EDT Updated: Mar 22, 2026 / 12:15 AM EDT RICHMOND, Va. (WRIC) — The VCU Rams’ NCAA tournament dreams have come to an end after falling 76-55 to Illinois in the second round on Saturday night. The Rams had already suffered a substantial loss just 46 seconds into the game as freshman starting guard Nyk Lewis came down and twisted his ankle after attempting to grab a rebound. Lewis left the game with assistance and did not return. Illinois would go on a run early, a three-pointer by Kylan Boswell giving them a 12-point lead around halfway through the first half. The Rams would respond with a 10-0 run capped off by a tip-in bucket by Tyrell Ward that would tie the game at 23. Later, Illinois’ Adrej Stojakovic would go on a 9-0 run by himself to end the first half to give them a 35-28 edge at the buzzer. The second half opened with back-to-back three-pointers by Illinois which would propel them to a double-digit lead just over one minute in. VCU’s offense struggled to finish at the rim, only shooting 34.8% from the field whereas Illinois shot 48.3%. The Fighting Illini bulldozed their way through the second half, advancing to the Sweet 16 with a 76-55 win. The first year of the Phil Martelli Jr. era at VCU concludes after the loss, with the Rams finishing the season 28-8 overall.",
